    basic: "Keep track of the Jacks! Since the Jack is a wild capture, don't drop a high-point card (like the 10 of Diamonds) into the center if your opponent hasn't played their Jacks yet. If you have the same rank as the top card, play it immediatelyâ€”don't 'Save' it, because the opponent might play a Jack and steal your match.",
    intermediate: "The 'Pişti' Setup: If you are the first player and the center card is something you have in your hand (e.g., an 8 is showing and you have an 8), play it. If the next person doesn't have an 8 or a Jack, you have a high chance of scoring a Pişti on your next turn. Memory is key: remember which ranks have been 'Clear' so you don't drop a card that can be 'Pish-teed'.",
    advanced: "The 'Endgame Vacuum': The winner of the very last trick gets all remaining cards in the center. In the final round of dealing, save your Jacks for the final two cards. This ensures that even if you didn't match anything mid-round, you can 'Sweep' the table for the 'Most Cards' bonus, which is often the tie-breaker for the 151 goal.",
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "The 10 of Diamonds (3 pts) and 2 of Clubs (2 pts) are the 'Gold' cards. Protect them!",
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "If you suspect your opponent has a Jack, lead a 'Low' card (like a 4 or 5) to lure their Jack out on a useless pile.",
      },
